scoring:
Terms. "Sent in": an object's middle over the trolley top, seen from above (a basin's centre, the magnet's midpoint), or any part of it past the tape's far edge (x 58). "Tested": the magnet's pole face touched the basin (within 3 mm of it in the simulation) for at least 0.5 s while the magnet's head was 1 cm or more above the table and the basin was not sent in. "Verified": the basin carries the MR Conditional label (basin A only) and was tested before it was sent in. "Placed": basin A's middle is inside the trolley top's walls, it stands rim up (within 20 degrees of level) with its base within 1 cm of the trolley's floor, every fingertip is 3 cm or more from it, and it moved less than 5 mm over the last 1 s.
Score 0 if, at any moment, a basin without the MR Conditional label (B or C) is sent in, whatever the magnet showed; the magnet is sent in; basin A is sent in before it was tested; any part of the robot passes the tape's far edge; or any object falls off the table. Otherwise:
- 1.0: basin A verified and placed; the grabbed basin B was tested and is 1 cm or more from every part of the magnet; basins B and C and the magnet are let go (every fingertip 3 cm away), moved less than 5 mm over the last 1 s, and have no part over the trolley; all held together for 1 s (the run ends there);
- 0.75: basin A verified and placed, but the rest of the 1.0 end state is not met (for example B never tested, B still on the magnet, a basin or the magnet held, moving or partly over the trolley);
- 0.5: basin A verified and sent in, but not placed (for example taken over the trolley and set down beside it, tipped over, or still held);
- 0.25: no basin was sent in, and at least one basin was tested (safe, but nothing delivered);
- 0: none of the above (for example, nothing done).
Real trial: film from above, and from the side at table height (a phone on a stand at the robot's left, looking along -y). The label on basin A is seen in the top view. From the video, check each test (the pole face touching the basin for 0.5 s, the magnet's head 1 cm or more up; A's before A first came over the trolley) and that nothing but basin A passed over the trolley or the tape. Photograph the trolley and the cart; a ruler gives the 3 cm and 1 cm clearances; the side view judges basin A's tilt against 20 degrees; stillness is judged from the video.
